<% @title = "Sponsors & contributors — Amber Framework" %>
<% @meta = "Meet the people and organizations investing time, engineering, and funding in Amber Framework." %>

<header class="page-hero community-hero">
  <div class="site-container page-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source is a group project</p>
      <h1>Backed by people<br>who keep showing up.</h1>
      <p>Amber exists because maintainers, contributors, sponsors, and users invest in the unglamorous work too: tests, releases, documentation, review, and long-term stewardship.</p>
    </div>
    <%= image_tag("characters/amber-chibi-hero-mark-v2.webp", class: "guide-amber", width: "520", height: "520", alt: "Amber giving a welcoming peace sign") %>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Main sponsor</p><h2>AgentC Consulting</h2></div>
        <p>AgentC Consulting funds and contributes engineering, design, documentation, release infrastructure, and ongoing stewardship for Amber V2.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="sponsor-feature reveal">
        <div class="sponsor-crystal" aria-hidden="true"><%= image_tag("brand/amber-crystal.svg", width: "88", height: "118", alt: "") %></div>
        <div>
          <span class="file-label">Primary project sponsor</span>
          <h2>Software should be clear enough to trust.</h2>
          <p>AgentC Consulting works with teams on product engineering and practical AI systems. Its sponsorship helps Amber turn that same standard of clarity into a public framework, a reproducible release path, and documentation that tells developers exactly where every piece belongs.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://agentc.consulting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit AgentC Consulting</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tinted">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Contributors</p><h2>The history is in the work.</h2></div>
        <p>GitHub keeps the complete, attribution-preserving record. These links include code, documentation, review, design, release, and maintenance contributions across Amber's core projects.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="contributor-grid">
        <article class="community-card reveal">
          <span class="file-label">Framework</span>
          <h3>Amber core</h3>
          <p>Routing, controllers, middleware, rendering, runtime behavior, tests, and the public framework API.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/amberframework/amber/graphs/contributors" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See framework contributors →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="community-card reveal">
          <span class="file-label">Developer tools</span>
          <h3>Amber CLI</h3>
          <p>Application templates, generators, release tooling, language-server support, and the first-run experience.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/amberframework/amber_cli/graphs/contributors" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See CLI contributors →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="community-card reveal">
          <span class="file-label">Public home</span>
          <h3>Website and docs</h3>
          <p>The open-source Amber application you are using now: ECR views, local assets, guides, examples, and release evidence.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/crimson-knight/amberframework.org/graphs/contributors" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See site contributors →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container community-invite reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Join the crew</p>
        <h2>There is useful work at every scale.</h2>
        <p>Report a confusing sentence, improve an example, test a platform, fix a bug, or help review the next release. A small, well-explained contribution is valuable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="community-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/amberframework/amber/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find an issue</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://discord.gg/vwvP5zakSn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Talk with the community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
